<title>UK: EIB sets 500 mln stg Eurobond due December 2007.</title>
<headline>EIB sets 500 mln stg Eurobond due December 2007.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager BZW.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    500 MLN STG   COUPON     **	  MATURITY    07.DEC.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    07.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER.</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.25 PCT GILT DUE DEC.2007</p>
<p> NOTES	CARRIES CLAUSE ALLOWING EIB TO REDENOMINATE ISSUE IN</p>
<p>		EUROS IF/WHEN BRITAIN ADOPTS THE EURO.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
